mac80211: bound the RX tasklet so a slow CPU cannot livelock

ieee80211_handle_queued_frames() drains local->skb_queue in an unbounded
while-loop. From the tasklet that is a livelock waiting to happen: if frames
arrive at least as fast as they are retired, the loop never exits, softirq
processing never yields, and userspace never runs again.

This board hits it every time. rtl_pci calls _rtl_pci_rx_interrupt() straight
from the hard IRQ handler and processes up to a whole RX ring (512 entries in
this tree) per interrupt, calling ieee80211_rx_irqsafe() for each frame -- so
frames land on the queue in large bursts from hard IRQ context, while this
tasklet retires them one at a time on a 400 MHz single-core MIPS. Bringing an
AP up on a busy 2.4 GHz channel wedges the box within seconds:

  watchdog: BUG: soft lockup - CPU#0 stuck for 23s! [hostapd:55]
  #1: 0% system, 100% softirq, 0% hardirq, 0% idle
  epc : arch_local_irq_enable+0x14/0x24
  ra  : handle_softirqs+0x9c/0x2e8

Give the tasklet path a budget: retire at most 64 frames, then reschedule and
return so other softirqs and userspace get the CPU. Throughput is unchanged --
the work still drains at full rate, just in bounded batches.

ieee80211_handle_queued_frames() keeps its drain-everything semantics for
ieee80211_stop_device(), which needs the queue actually emptied.

--- a/net/mac80211/main.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/main.c
@@ -439,7 +439,13 @@
 }
 
 /* context: requires softirqs disabled */
-void ieee80211_handle_queued_frames(struct ieee80211_local *local)
+/*
+ * Process queued frames, at most @budget of them; @budget == 0 means "drain
+ * everything". Returns true if the queues were emptied, false if the budget
+ * ran out with frames possibly still queued.
+ */
+static bool __ieee80211_handle_queued_frames(struct ieee80211_local *local,
+					     unsigned int budget)
 {
 	struct sk_buff *skb;
 
@@ -462,14 +468,37 @@
 			dev_kfree_skb(skb);
 			break;
 		}
+
+		if (budget && --budget == 0)
+			return false;
 	}
+
+	return true;
+}
+
+void ieee80211_handle_queued_frames(struct ieee80211_local *local)
+{
+	__ieee80211_handle_queued_frames(local, 0);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Frames per tasklet run before yielding. Draining the queue unbounded here
+ * livelocks a slow CPU: on a 400 MHz RTL8196E in AP mode the driver hands
+ * frames up from hard IRQ context (rtl_pci processes a whole 512-entry RX ring
+ * per interrupt) faster than this tasklet can retire them, so the loop never
+ * exits, softirq processing never yields, and the box wedges at 100% softirq
+ * until the softlockup watchdog panics it. Yield and reschedule instead: the
+ * work still drains at full rate, but userspace and other softirqs get to run.
+ */
+#define IEEE80211_RX_TASKLET_BUDGET	64
+
 static void ieee80211_tasklet_handler(struct tasklet_struct *t)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_local *local = from_tasklet(local, t, tasklet);
 
-	ieee80211_handle_queued_frames(local);
+	if (!__ieee80211_handle_queued_frames(local,
+					      IEEE80211_RX_TASKLET_BUDGET))
+		tasklet_schedule(&local->tasklet);
 }
 
 static void ieee80211_restart_work(struct work_struct *work)
